  "worked_solution": "The range of ${(1.5)}^{x}$ is\n\n$$\n{(1.5)}^{x}>0.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches do not affect the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{(1.5)}^{2x}>0.\n$$\n\nSubtracting  $0.5$ from the above inequality yields the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(1.5)}^{2x} & >0 \\\\ {(1.5)}^{2x}-0.5 & >0-0.5 \\\\ f(x) & >-0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range is $f(x)>-0.5.$ Thus, of the given values, only $y=0$ and $y=-0.2$ are outputs of $y=f(x).$\n\nWe can also see that this is true from the graph of the function. The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943819/assets/5876d2095bfd91417d2e6395f8a02ae817ebd476076bae929d79709ea7961a3e.png)\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
